    "gold_solution": "```python\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"Disaster_Response_Logistics\")\n    m.setParam(\"TimeLimit\", 300)  # Set time limit to 300 seconds\n\n    # Data\n    depots = list(range(3))  # D0..D2\n    units = list(range(4))  # U0..U3\n    supplies = list(range(2))  # S0..S1\n    days = list(range(1))  # Day0..Day0\n\n    demands = [[[27.66], [21.99]], [[19.85], [49.13]], [[36.57], [45.92]], [[23.88], [26.81]]]\n    depot_supplies = [[[43.21], [45.14]], [[53.02], [45.06]], [[45.6], [42.36]]]\n    transport_costs = [[4.82, 1.06, 3.16, 2.96], [4.94, 4.93, 1.45, 1.1], [2.4, 1.39, 2.42, 3.09]]\n    risk_costs = [[194.98, 142.38, 54.37, 139.65], [63.28, 186.57, 92.3, 105.4], [67.56, 129.91, 84.63, 151.45]]\n    supply_volumes = [1.77, 1.71]\n    penalty_costs = [85.33, 65.23]\n    vehicle_cost = 10.0\n    vehicle_capacity = 100.0\n    total_vehicles = 20\n\n    # Decision variables\n    # Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Amount of supply s from depot d to unit u on day t\n    flows = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                for s in supplies:\n                    flows[(d, u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Flow_D{d}_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}: Shortage of supply s at unit u on day t\n    slacks = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                slacks[(u, s, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Slack_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Number of vehicles on route d->u on day t\n    vehicles = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                vehicles[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(lb=0.0, vtype=GRB.INTEGER, name=f\"Veh_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}: Route d->u is active on day t (binary)\n    routes = {}\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                routes[(d, u, t)] = m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"Route_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\")\n\n    # Objective: Minimize total cost (transport + penalty + vehicle + risk)\n    obj = quicksum(\n        transport_costs[d][u] * flows[(d, u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        penalty_costs[s] * slacks[(u, s, t)]\n        for t in days for u in units for s in supplies\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        vehicle_cost * vehicles[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    obj += quicksum(\n        risk_costs[d][u] * routes[(d, u, t)]\n        for t in days for d in depots for u in units\n    )\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # Depot capacity constraints: Total outflow <= supply\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for u in units) <= depot_supplies[d][s][t],\n                    name=f\"DepotCap_D{d}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Demand constraints: Inflow + slack >= demand\n    for t in days:\n        for u in units:\n            for s in supplies:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(flows[(d, u, s, t)] for d in depots) + slacks[(u, s, t)] >= demands[u][s][t],\n                    name=f\"Demand_U{u}_S{s}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Vehicle capacity constraints: Total volume <= vehicles * capacity\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    quicksum(supply_volumes[s] * flows[(d, u, s, t)] for s in supplies) <= vehicle_capacity * vehicles[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"VehCap_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Route activation constraints: vehicles <= total_vehicles * route\n    for t in days:\n        for d in depots:\n            for u in units:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    vehicles[(d, u, t)] <= total_vehicles * routes[(d, u, t)],\n                    name=f\"RouteAct_D{d}_U{u}_Day{t}\"\n                )\n\n    # Fleet size constraints: Total vehicles <= total_vehicles\n    for t in days:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(vehicles[(d, u, t)] for d in depots for u in units) <= total_vehicles,\n            name=f\"FleetSize_Day{t}\"\n        )\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "Situation:\nA sudden-onset disaster has disrupted overland access across the central corridor. Supply Depot Alpha (seaport), Supply Depot Bravo (inland logistics hub), and Forward Depot Charlie (airhead) remain operational with constrained stocks and handling capacity. Supported elements include the 1st Field Hospital Falcon, the 3rd Relief Battalion, WASH Task Force Echo, and Shelter Support Company Delta, dispersed across damaged road networks and intermittent communications. Several corridors traverse unstable terrain and areas with security incidents; route clearance and escort teams are required to move convoys. Activating any corridor (sending any vehicles between a depot and a receiving unit) triggers a fixed Risk Cost for security and clearance overheads, irrespective of how many vehicles use the route.\n\nMission:\nDeliver critical supplies to supported units during the current operational period while minimizing total operational cost (transport, shortage penalties, vehicle deployment, and fixed route security Risk Costs) and maintaining responder safety.\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Flows will be assigned from each depot to each supported unit by supply type. Dispatch from any depot cannot exceed its available stock per supply and period.\n- Each unit\u2019s demand must be covered to the extent possible; any shortfall is recorded as unmet need and penalized to reflect humanitarian impact.\n- Vehicle capacity is enforced using per-unit supply volumes; total volume dispatched on a lane must fit within the number of vehicles allocated to that lane and the vehicle capacity.\n- A lane becomes active only if vehicles are assigned; vehicles may not operate on inactive lanes. Activating any lane incurs a fixed Risk Cost to account for escorts, route clearance, and movement control, regardless of convoy size.\n- Total vehicles in service across all lanes are limited by the available fleet. Each vehicle deployed incurs a use cost.\n- Transport costs apply to moving supply along each lane. The planning tool will minimize the sum of transport costs, unmet-demand penalties, per-vehicle costs, and fixed Risk Costs for each activated lane.\n- Operational priorities: open the minimum set of safe, essential corridors; concentrate movements on lower-risk, higher-throughput lanes; sequence deliveries to life-saving functions first; and hold a reserve for contingency diversions. Movements will be synchronized with route clearance teams and force protection elements, with dynamic rerouting if conditions degrade.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\nUnit Demands (Units x Supplies):\nUnit\\Supply | S 0 | S 1\n-----------------------\nU 0        |  27.66 |  21.99\nU 1        |  19.85 |  49.13\nU 2        |  36.57 |  45.92\nU 3        |  23.88 |  26.81\nDepot Supplies (Depots x Supplies):\nDepot\\Supply | S 0 | S 1\n------------------------\nD 0        |  43.21 |  45.14\nD 1        |  53.02 |  45.06\nD 2        |  45.60 |  42.36\nTransport Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2 | U 3\n----------------------------------\nD 0        |   4.82 |   1.06 |   3.16 |   2.96\nD 1        |   4.94 |   4.93 |   1.45 |   1.10\nD 2        |   2.40 |   1.39 |   2.42 |   3.09\nRisk Costs (Depot x Unit):\nDepot\\Unit | U 0 | U 1 | U 2 | U 3\n----------------------------------\nD 0        | 194.98 | 142.38 |  54.37 | 139.65\nD 1        |  63.28 | 186.57 |  92.30 | 105.40\nD 2        |  67.56 | 129.91 |  84.63 | 151.45\nPenalty Costs per Unit Shortage: [Supply S0: 85.33, Supply S1: 65.23]\nVolume per Supply Unit: [Supply S0: 1.77, Supply S1: 1.71]\nFleet Parameters: Cost 10.0, Capacity 100.0, Total 20",
    "LLM_description_template": "Situation:\nA sudden-onset disaster has disrupted overland access across the central corridor. Supply Depot Alpha (seaport), Supply Depot Bravo (inland logistics hub), and Forward Depot Charlie (airhead) remain operational with constrained stocks and handling capacity. Supported elements include the 1st Field Hospital Falcon, the 3rd Relief Battalion, WASH Task Force Echo, and Shelter Support Company Delta, dispersed across damaged road networks and intermittent communications. Several corridors traverse unstable terrain and areas with security incidents; route clearance and escort teams are required to move convoys. Activating any corridor (sending any vehicles between a depot and a receiving unit) triggers a fixed Risk Cost for security and clearance overheads, irrespective of how many vehicles use the route.\n\nMission:\nDeliver critical supplies to supported units during the current operational period while minimizing total operational cost (transport, shortage penalties, vehicle deployment, and fixed route security Risk Costs) and maintaining responder safety.\n\nExecution/Concept:\n- Flows will be assigned from each depot to each supported unit by supply type. Dispatch from any depot cannot exceed its available stock per supply and period.\n- Each unit\u2019s demand must be covered to the extent possible; any shortfall is recorded as unmet need and penalized to reflect humanitarian impact.\n- Vehicle capacity is enforced using per-unit supply volumes; total volume dispatched on a lane must fit within the number of vehicles allocated to that lane and the vehicle capacity.\n- A lane becomes active only if vehicles are assigned; vehicles may not operate on inactive lanes. Activating any lane incurs a fixed Risk Cost to account for escorts, route clearance, and movement control, regardless of convoy size.\n- Total vehicles in service across all lanes are limited by the available fleet. Each vehicle deployed incurs a use cost.\n- Transport costs apply to moving supply along each lane. The planning tool will minimize the sum of transport costs, unmet-demand penalties, per-vehicle costs, and fixed Risk Costs for each activated lane.\n- Operational priorities: open the minimum set of safe, essential corridors; concentrate movements on lower-risk, higher-throughput lanes; sequence deliveries to life-saving functions first; and hold a reserve for contingency diversions. Movements will be synchronized with route clearance teams and force protection elements, with dynamic rerouting if conditions degrade.\n\nAnnex A - Logistics Data:\n{DEMANDS}\n{DEPOT_SUPPLIES}\n{TRANSPORT_COSTS}\n{RISK_COSTS}\n{PENALTY_COSTS}\n{SUPPLY_VOLUMES}\nFleet Parameters: Cost {VEHICLE_COST}, Capacity {VEHICLE_CAPACITY}, Total {TOTAL_VEHICLES}"
